WEBVTT

00:45.128 --> 00:47.047
Where are we going?

00:47.130 --> 00:50.008
- Shut up and come on.
- Why were all those people there?

00:50.091 --> 00:52.385
I saw that bastard Lee Si…

00:53.136 --> 00:54.554
You're in no place to ask questions.

00:54.637 --> 00:56.723
You burst into my home
in the middle of night causing drama.

00:56.806 --> 00:57.932
Why? Tell me why!

00:58.892 --> 01:00.935
Uh, Ha-kyung…

01:01.519 --> 01:03.104
You're being scary.

01:03.188 --> 01:06.357
You think? You showed up drunk
on my doorstep and you're scared of me?

01:09.069 --> 01:11.071
Yeah, you should be happy.

01:11.154 --> 01:14.199
I'm here, 'cause I wanted
to apologize to you.

01:14.824 --> 01:16.326
What?

01:17.827 --> 01:19.954
It's all my fault, Ha-kyung.

01:23.875 --> 01:24.876
Sorry.

01:25.585 --> 01:26.795
I'm so sorry.

01:27.420 --> 01:30.548
I really need you to know that.

01:32.842 --> 01:35.929
I'm a real asshole. I know it.

01:41.142 --> 01:43.186
They called off their wedding,
isn't that right?

01:44.104 --> 01:45.105
Yeah.

01:46.314 --> 01:47.690
Why did he come here, then?

01:48.399 --> 01:49.317
Don't know.

01:52.362 --> 01:54.030
He was drunk, I think.

01:54.114 --> 01:55.615
I could check if they're okay.

01:57.575 --> 01:58.827
I'd leave them alone.

02:01.788 --> 02:03.123
I'm gonna go find them.

02:09.963 --> 02:11.256
I'm going home.

02:12.465 --> 02:13.633
Seok-ho.

02:15.969 --> 02:17.720
Your apartment's right up upstairs?

02:17.804 --> 02:19.097
Yes. Why?

02:19.180 --> 02:20.265
Mm.

02:22.433 --> 02:23.893
Well, actually…

02:25.603 --> 02:28.773
It feels weird sleeping here.
So maybe I could--

02:28.857 --> 02:31.359
- That's not weird. You'll get used to it.
- You think? That's good.

02:31.442 --> 02:33.236
- Oh, yeah. See you at work.
- Mm.

02:33.319 --> 02:34.612
Okay. Bye.

02:37.240 --> 02:39.117
You shoved me down so fast.

02:48.126 --> 02:50.336
Are you hurting? Was it painful?

02:52.505 --> 02:54.132
What are you saying?

03:01.472 --> 03:04.434
When you saw that I betrayed you,

03:05.393 --> 03:06.769
did you feel like so insecure

03:06.853 --> 03:10.815
that your heart threw it on the ground
and stomps on it a million times?

03:11.608 --> 03:12.442
Oh, no.

03:12.525 --> 03:14.360
It wasn't pain.

03:14.444 --> 03:17.572
Humiliation, that was the bigger thing
I had to get through.

03:18.489 --> 03:21.743
So if you could stop finding ways
to embarrass me, that'd be great, huh?

03:25.371 --> 03:27.290
I understand.

03:28.666 --> 03:31.753
My love Ha-kyung was embarrassed…

03:32.503 --> 03:35.673
That happens when you lie.

03:37.508 --> 03:39.177
Hey. Come on.

03:39.719 --> 03:42.096
What the hell is wrong with you today?

03:42.680 --> 03:43.765
Ha-kyung.

03:44.807 --> 03:47.352
I think something's punishing me.

03:47.435 --> 03:48.394
What?

03:49.520 --> 03:52.982
I'm being punished,
because I hurt and betrayed you.

03:58.363 --> 04:00.240
Hey, it's in the past.

04:00.323 --> 04:02.533
And your tantrum
won't make me proofread your article.

04:03.243 --> 04:05.787
Lee Si-woo, it's all his fault.

04:06.955 --> 04:09.040
He did it to Yu-jin, you know?

04:09.874 --> 04:13.169
He lived with her,
she didn't even know me, but still…

04:14.128 --> 04:16.464
What am I supposed to do now, Ha-kyung?

04:17.715 --> 04:20.510
I sacrificed a lot for the wedding.

04:22.679 --> 04:28.726
I hurt you so much, I didn't mean to
became the biggest jerk to have her.

04:30.061 --> 04:32.647
I just happened to be the biggest jerk.

04:33.523 --> 04:39.362
How could she go and lie to me like that?
She didn't even wanna tell the truth.

04:41.364 --> 04:42.907
She didn't really lie.

04:44.117 --> 04:46.286
But she sure did a good job
of not telling you.

04:47.161 --> 04:49.539
At the end of the day, though,
you're married.

04:49.622 --> 04:51.291
Would she be upset if she saw

04:51.374 --> 04:54.002
how you're acting
over something she did so long ago?

04:55.753 --> 04:59.549
If you love someone,
you have to accept all of them.

04:59.632 --> 05:01.134
Good and bad, and move on.

05:03.845 --> 05:05.013
Understand, Ki-jun?

05:06.431 --> 05:08.725
You're sleeping?

05:09.559 --> 05:10.560
Hey.

05:12.562 --> 05:13.396
Hey!

05:14.522 --> 05:15.857
What the hell? Wake up!

05:15.940 --> 05:19.569
This isn't okay!

05:21.029 --> 05:22.530
Oh, God.

05:24.490 --> 05:25.658
Lee Si-woo.

05:25.742 --> 05:27.535
You don't know where he lives, do you?

05:29.662 --> 05:31.039
I don't. I have no idea.

05:49.265 --> 05:50.892
Mmm.

05:56.647 --> 06:02.403
LEE SI-WOO

06:08.493 --> 06:09.619
Hello?

06:10.203 --> 06:11.662
Why are you calling so late?

06:30.640 --> 06:31.599
Oppa?

06:33.101 --> 06:34.560
I'm sorry.

06:35.395 --> 06:36.896
I'm so sorry.

06:37.939 --> 06:39.107
How did this…

06:41.275 --> 06:42.944
How did you… Why are you driving him home?

06:43.736 --> 06:45.613
Your husband can answer better than I can.

06:47.448 --> 06:48.783
- Gosh.
- Here.

06:58.334 --> 06:59.460
Okay. I got him.

07:00.461 --> 07:02.547
What were you thinking? You're so drunk.

07:03.548 --> 07:04.465
Ki-jun.

07:05.216 --> 07:07.260
We're going home. Okay?

07:08.803 --> 07:10.221
Wake up and walk.

07:14.642 --> 07:16.811
Why did you go get drunk?

07:18.604 --> 07:19.856
I'm sorry.

07:20.815 --> 07:21.899
I'm sorry.

07:22.400 --> 07:23.776
I bet you are sorry.

07:25.236 --> 07:27.447
I'm so sorry.

07:28.030 --> 07:29.407
Ha-kyung.

07:32.368 --> 07:33.703
My fault.

07:34.954 --> 07:37.832
So, so sorry, Jin Ha-kyung.

08:29.509 --> 08:32.512
Bad weather isn't
as obvious as cloudy skies,

08:32.595 --> 08:37.183
unexpected snow and rain,
strong wind, and typhoons.

08:37.266 --> 08:38.726
It can be more subtle.

08:45.525 --> 08:46.859
Why are you still out here?

08:48.653 --> 08:50.238
So you got him back home all right?

08:51.614 --> 08:54.075
I'm sorry, you shouldn't have to do that.

08:54.867 --> 08:56.035
Let's go in.

08:56.118 --> 08:57.912
Does it bother you that much too?

08:58.496 --> 08:59.455
Does what?

09:00.498 --> 09:04.043
That Yu-jin and I were living together?

09:04.126 --> 09:06.712
Even just
hot weather and humidity

09:06.796 --> 09:08.965
hold people down and affect their moods.

09:09.048 --> 09:10.925
I heard Han Ki-jun talk about it.

09:11.509 --> 09:12.969
Does it bother you like that too?

09:17.390 --> 09:18.474
Well…

09:19.183 --> 09:21.018
I wouldn't say I feel like Han Ki-jun.

09:22.228 --> 09:24.355
But it did sting a little bit.

09:25.481 --> 09:28.484
Like when I found out
about you writing all

09:28.568 --> 09:30.861
of Han Ki-jun's columns for him,
and that you still do?

09:30.945 --> 09:32.446
Heat and humidity…

09:32.530 --> 09:33.489
Is it like that?

09:33.573 --> 09:35.408
…does it put people
more on edge than usual?

09:35.491 --> 09:36.826
Who told you that?

09:39.161 --> 09:40.621
I heard it at work.

09:40.705 --> 09:43.583
- Why didn't you mention it?
- You didn't mention it, either, so…

09:43.666 --> 09:46.544
People become combative in heat.

09:46.627 --> 09:48.588
It only seems
like you want to fight with me.

09:48.671 --> 09:50.673
You can at least try to just fight.

09:51.507 --> 09:53.926
Just like that,
we've been transformed,

09:54.010 --> 09:58.431
irritable and unaware
that it's the weather's doing.

10:30.755 --> 10:31.922
Oh…

10:42.642 --> 10:44.935
God, it's so hot.

10:45.519 --> 10:52.485
EPISODE 8
DISCOMFORT INDEX

11:45.705 --> 11:47.123
What happened last night?

11:50.084 --> 11:51.168
What do you mean?

11:52.044 --> 11:53.796
You were totally wasted,

11:53.879 --> 11:56.882
and for some reason,
Lee Si-woo had to bring you home.

11:56.966 --> 11:59.635
- What was that?
- Let's talk later.

11:59.719 --> 12:02.596
I need to know what happened.
You have to tell me right now.

12:05.683 --> 12:07.685
There's no time right now, Yu-jin.

12:09.270 --> 12:12.106
What's wrong? Was it something I did?

12:15.067 --> 12:16.777
I just…

12:17.528 --> 12:19.447
…need some space to think this through.

12:20.072 --> 12:21.198
I'm going to work.

12:33.294 --> 12:34.295
Wait…

12:36.213 --> 12:39.300
You took… I was going
to clean it this morning.

12:39.383 --> 12:42.428
Let's make a rule
that a food gets cleaned up after eating.

12:42.511 --> 12:44.555
If we don't, the apartment
will absorb the smell.

12:44.638 --> 12:46.766
Of course. I will in the future.

12:49.393 --> 12:50.770
Hey, how did you…

12:51.353 --> 12:55.274
You can find ready-made food on top left.
Plates and things are on the right.

12:55.357 --> 12:59.069
Perishables like bread and milk
are obviously in the fridge.

12:59.153 --> 13:00.321
So please help yourselves.

13:00.404 --> 13:01.781
I'll see you both at work.

13:03.574 --> 13:05.034
Please, have breakfast.

13:05.117 --> 13:06.327
Okay. See you.

13:07.119 --> 13:09.079
We'll be there soon.

13:16.045 --> 13:17.671
Do you want ramen?

13:17.755 --> 13:19.215
- Huh?
- She said have some.

13:20.090 --> 13:22.218
Oh, the ramen is over here.

13:23.928 --> 13:24.929
Over here.

13:25.012 --> 13:27.223
And the pot…

13:27.973 --> 13:31.310
- is here.
- Huh?

13:32.311 --> 13:34.063
How did you know that?

13:34.855 --> 13:35.981
Oh.

13:36.065 --> 13:38.526
I just listened.
She just pointed everything out.

13:39.109 --> 13:40.611
- Oh.
- Yeah.

13:42.238 --> 13:44.573
I'll boil water for us. Okay.

13:46.909 --> 13:50.204
Oh, it's only morning, and it's so hot.

13:50.287 --> 13:52.081
- I'm gonna go shower.
- Okay.

13:58.838 --> 14:03.342
This afternoon, we're expecting
the temperature to rise to 30° in Seoul.

14:03.425 --> 14:04.677
Humidity will stay high.

14:04.760 --> 14:08.013
The current discomfort index
in Seoul is 76.7.

14:08.097 --> 14:09.723
So everyone should keep an eye out,

14:09.807 --> 14:12.560
for those feeling moody
from the humidity and heat.

14:13.143 --> 14:15.896
Even though the temperature is almost
the same as the last few days,

14:15.980 --> 14:18.440
the higher humidity
will affect our perception,

14:18.524 --> 14:20.609
so the heat today will feel
even more stifling.

14:20.693 --> 14:24.113
Highest today will be 31° in Seoul,
30 in Cheongju.

14:24.196 --> 14:27.199
Like when I found out
about you writing all

14:27.283 --> 14:29.618
of Han Ki-jun's columns for him,
and that you still do?

14:30.202 --> 14:31.662
Is it like that?

14:45.968 --> 14:47.219
What the…

15:07.489 --> 15:08.490
Miss Kim.

15:08.991 --> 15:10.576
- This is the data.
- Morning.

15:10.659 --> 15:12.870
- Hi.
- Good morning.

15:13.662 --> 15:15.289
Good morning.

15:35.809 --> 15:36.894
Oh, thank you.

15:37.478 --> 15:39.229
Hey, it's hot in here, right?

15:39.980 --> 15:42.524
Is it? I don't think so.

15:43.275 --> 15:46.278
You spend too much time with the data
saying you would feel warmer today.

15:48.030 --> 15:51.533
Or you might be nervous,
because we'll have monsoon soon.

15:51.617 --> 15:52.618
Seriously?

15:53.410 --> 15:54.620
It's getting warm in here.

15:55.245 --> 15:56.163
I told you.

16:01.418 --> 16:02.795
I'm gonna call someone.

16:06.548 --> 16:08.926
Hello, this is the Chief Team
of the Forecast Bureau.

16:09.009 --> 16:10.970
It seems like there's an issue
with our AC unit.

16:11.637 --> 16:13.347
Oh, for real?

16:15.099 --> 16:16.475
We're starting the meeting soon.

16:17.518 --> 16:19.895
Okay. Please do it as soon as possible.

16:22.356 --> 16:24.358
- Hey.
- Hello, sir.

16:25.901 --> 16:27.569
Are we not running the AC?

16:27.653 --> 16:29.655
There's a problem
with the AC in the whole building,

16:29.738 --> 16:32.491
but, um, they dispatched
the Repair Team to fix it.

16:32.574 --> 16:35.369
Oh, not today, of all this.

16:35.452 --> 16:36.370
Okay.

16:37.371 --> 16:39.081
Shouldn't Director Jin be here?

16:40.582 --> 16:41.625
I don't know.

16:42.501 --> 16:44.712
She left before we did, so…

16:44.795 --> 16:45.754
Yeah.

16:54.555 --> 16:55.973
Hey, Ha-kyung. What do you need?

16:56.056 --> 16:58.267
My car insurance
is Areumhaesang, isn't it?

16:58.350 --> 16:59.768
I changed it.

16:59.852 --> 17:02.021
I moved it over to the company
that Sang-hun works for.

17:02.104 --> 17:03.814
What? And you didn't let me know?

17:08.777 --> 17:09.737
Hey.

17:09.820 --> 17:11.488
You're calling your insurance or what?

17:11.572 --> 17:13.407
What do you think I'm doing right now?

17:14.450 --> 17:16.118
Okay. What's this company called?

17:16.702 --> 17:18.996
- Oh, come on. I don't have all day--
- Yes, I'm aware!

17:20.956 --> 17:22.541
So where are you? I'll take my car.

17:22.624 --> 17:23.542
No, don't.

17:23.625 --> 17:25.794
Just give me the name for the company.

17:25.878 --> 17:29.048
I'll handle it for you.
I'm coming now to meet up with you.

17:30.132 --> 17:33.218
The person you are trying
to reach is not available at this time.

17:33.302 --> 17:34.344
Please try again.

17:38.140 --> 17:39.016
Okay.

17:39.683 --> 17:42.853
Do what you have to do. All right. Mm-hm.

17:43.812 --> 17:45.147
- Sir.
- Hm?

17:45.230 --> 17:47.816
Director Jin got in a car accident
on her way here.

17:47.900 --> 17:49.276
What?

17:51.528 --> 17:52.654
Well, is she okay?

17:52.738 --> 17:54.531
Yeah, she's all right.

17:54.615 --> 17:56.492
Anyway, I can sit in for her. Okay?

17:56.575 --> 17:57.576
Okay.

17:59.953 --> 18:03.624
On today of all days
when we've got an important briefing.

18:03.707 --> 18:08.128
Is this a bad sign for the season?

18:08.212 --> 18:09.880
Don't jinx it.

18:10.672 --> 18:12.966
It's just the weather
putting everyone on edge.

18:13.509 --> 18:15.344
Don't read into it too much, Miss Kim.

18:15.427 --> 18:16.345
Okay.

18:23.602 --> 18:25.646
Hey, uh, shouldn't Mr. Han be here?

18:25.729 --> 18:29.399
Uh, he said something came up.
He told me to fill in for him today.

18:39.118 --> 18:41.537
Let's commence
the forecast discussion for June 27.

18:41.620 --> 18:42.913
Satellite Center, you there?

18:43.497 --> 18:46.458
Yes, if you look at the satellite image
and this chart,

18:46.542 --> 18:50.254
there's a stationary front of waves out
over the sea by the Southern Jeju.

18:51.046 --> 18:52.631
I heard you got in an accident.

18:53.215 --> 18:54.800
Please call me when you can.

18:59.972 --> 19:03.183
Since no one got hurt,
insurance should cover it all. Easy.

19:03.267 --> 19:05.144
- Thank you, sir.
- Just sign right here.

19:05.227 --> 19:06.145
Okay.

19:10.065 --> 19:12.067
All right. I'll call you later
about the car.

19:43.140 --> 19:45.267
What are you doing here?
I said not to come.

19:45.350 --> 19:47.269
I was on the phone with Sang-hun
on my way over,

19:47.352 --> 19:50.397
and he said he'll do
the necessary paperwork and everything,

19:50.480 --> 19:51.607
and call you later.

19:51.690 --> 19:54.234
Why did you change
my insurance without telling me?

19:54.318 --> 19:56.445
It's made this whole thing way harder.

19:56.528 --> 19:57.696
My bad.

19:57.779 --> 20:00.240
It's 'cause I thought we'd only have
one car after we got married.

20:00.324 --> 20:02.743
Mine expired,
and I wanted to help my friend.

20:03.243 --> 20:05.120
If I knew where we were headed,
I wouldn't have--

20:05.204 --> 20:07.414
You always do this, you know?
You're impulsive.

20:07.497 --> 20:09.958
You do whatever you want,
and then I have to clean it up.

20:10.042 --> 20:11.418
Well, I fixed this.

20:11.501 --> 20:13.545
Well, then good for you. You can go now.

20:13.629 --> 20:15.923
All right. Hop in now. We're already late.

20:16.673 --> 20:17.507
I'm okay.

20:18.342 --> 20:20.844
I told Mr. Um to handle all of that.

20:20.928 --> 20:22.346
I am late, but I'll get a taxi.

20:22.429 --> 20:23.430
- So I should--
- Huh?

20:23.931 --> 20:26.433
You think a taxi will pick you up
from down here?

20:30.729 --> 20:33.106
I HEARD YOU GOT IN AN ACCIDENT.
PLEASE CALL ME WHEN YOU CAN.

20:34.399 --> 20:38.487
In conclusion, we expect
the stationary fronts will cause rainfall

20:38.570 --> 20:41.323
in Southern Jeju, in five days from now.

20:41.406 --> 20:45.535
Ah, we'll keep an eye on the atmosphere
over the ocean. You just never know.

20:45.619 --> 20:48.705
'Cause if the front keeps going north
and then goes south,

20:48.789 --> 20:50.415
there's a chance the rain start later.

20:50.499 --> 20:53.627
The North Pacific anticyclone
is pulling in the Southeast.

20:53.710 --> 20:55.504
Otherwise, we would've
taken that into account.

20:55.587 --> 20:59.049
However, it's possible the rain
may come early, it just couldn't be later.

20:59.132 --> 21:00.801
If you look at Jeju Sea,

21:00.884 --> 21:02.970
the atmosphere looks like
it's hardly moving at all.

21:03.637 --> 21:06.807
If that trough doesn't maintain
its current altitude of five kilometers

21:06.890 --> 21:09.643
- or the North Pacific anticyclone…
- What happened?

21:09.726 --> 21:10.978
Hey. Are you okay?

21:11.061 --> 21:12.688
The front could shift.

21:12.771 --> 21:15.440
It could remain north-headed
and then fall back to the south.

21:15.524 --> 21:17.818
If the pressure system contributes,
and it maintains

21:17.901 --> 21:20.654
the five-kilometer altitude,
then it would be worth following.

21:21.530 --> 21:23.532
Jeju Office, let's hear from you.

21:23.615 --> 21:25.867
I agree
with the Busan Office.

21:25.951 --> 21:29.037
With that gale, at a 200hPa
above the north side

21:29.121 --> 21:33.125
 of the stationary front,
it's likely the rain will develop sooner.

21:35.460 --> 21:36.628
Hm…

21:39.006 --> 21:41.633
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

21:59.818 --> 22:01.570
Think about the public response.

22:01.653 --> 22:05.198
Imagine the criticism if it rains earlier,
and the public isn't prepared.

22:05.282 --> 22:07.617
With rain,
even when we're just a day late,

22:07.701 --> 22:09.995
the criticism is worse
than being days early.

22:10.787 --> 22:12.080
It's better to play it safe.

22:12.748 --> 22:15.042
Not when the data is this clear.

22:16.043 --> 22:18.670
We've seen our weather
get more and more fickle,

22:18.754 --> 22:20.130
because of climate change.

22:21.423 --> 22:22.924
Almost every year for several seasons,

22:23.008 --> 22:24.885
we missed the mark on the end
of monsoon season,

22:24.968 --> 22:26.720
even though we really tried.

22:26.803 --> 22:29.222
Almost no one trusts
the forecast any longer.

22:29.806 --> 22:33.101
So, if we get the first day
of the season wrong too,

22:34.102 --> 22:37.022
I can't even imagine the amount
of criticism we'd get from that.

22:37.105 --> 22:38.982
Do you think it's worth the risk?

22:42.319 --> 22:46.156
Well, then we could postpone
the announcement if we had to.

22:47.991 --> 22:50.827
- What's the rule? Can we do that?
- We've already postponed it quite a bit.

22:50.911 --> 22:53.372
Presses and local officials
are already calling

22:53.455 --> 22:55.582
that they were alerted
to the current conditions.

22:55.665 --> 22:57.501
So they really wanna know our thoughts.

22:57.584 --> 23:00.587
If we did, they'll have another excuse
to publish whatever.

23:00.670 --> 23:03.548
Don't you remember
how awful it went last time?

23:03.632 --> 23:05.050
Mr. Lee, thoughts?

23:13.558 --> 23:14.601
Lee Si-woo.

23:15.977 --> 23:17.020
What do you think?

23:27.656 --> 23:28.490
I apologize.

23:29.282 --> 23:30.909
I missed a little of what you were saying.

23:30.992 --> 23:32.285
You kidding?

23:33.453 --> 23:34.704
I'm sorry.

23:37.582 --> 23:39.251
Okay. What's the plan?

23:39.751 --> 23:42.087
Due to the trough
in northern central China,

23:42.170 --> 23:43.964
and the formation of the gale,

23:44.047 --> 23:46.258
there's a higher probability
that the stationary front

23:46.341 --> 23:47.717
will travel to the north, right?

23:48.427 --> 23:51.555
Do we expect rainfall
in the next five days or don't we?

23:52.931 --> 23:55.517
We have to. Yeah. Announce it, it's fine.

23:57.060 --> 23:58.812
- You're sure?
- Yes, sir.

24:02.941 --> 24:04.943
Okay. Well, get to it.

24:06.111 --> 24:09.239
Let's also prepare
for a press briefing this afternoon.

24:09.322 --> 24:11.241
Oh, also, at the briefing today,

24:11.324 --> 24:12.993
the Office of Spokesperson
should emphasize

24:13.076 --> 24:15.162
that the journalists should not
jump to conclusions

24:15.245 --> 24:17.122
or overstate any dates at all.

24:17.205 --> 24:19.040
- unlike what they did last year.
- Yes.

24:19.124 --> 24:21.084
Hm? Well done, everyone.

24:21.168 --> 24:23.837
- Thank you all.
- Thank you.

24:43.773 --> 24:46.651
- Who's covering you?
- Oh, Assistant Director Kim said he could.

24:47.444 --> 24:48.737
Well, that's fantastic.

24:53.158 --> 24:54.159
Sorry for yesterday.

24:55.118 --> 24:56.661
I drank way too much.

24:57.204 --> 24:58.788
Was it really bad?

25:00.790 --> 25:02.626
You already know, so why are you asking?

25:04.252 --> 25:06.004
I'm sorry.

25:07.214 --> 25:09.424
- You have to get over.
- Hm?

25:10.467 --> 25:11.968
- Turn signal.
- Oh.

25:19.184 --> 25:21.561
Some things don't ever change, right?

25:21.645 --> 25:22.812
I don't know.

25:27.734 --> 25:30.278
Ha-kyung, what am I gonna do?

25:31.780 --> 25:34.574
- Leave her if you have to.
- What? How can you even say that?

25:36.201 --> 25:37.410
I can't do that.

25:37.494 --> 25:39.246
I love her way too much to do that to her.

25:40.288 --> 25:41.289
Then just let it go.

25:41.873 --> 25:44.459
It's that guy, Lee Si-woo did this.

25:44.543 --> 25:46.920
What? No, it's not.
It's just between you and her.

25:47.546 --> 25:50.048
You're so defensive when Lee Si-woo
comes up. What's with you?

25:51.258 --> 25:53.510
It's not him. It's about you
blaming things on him.

25:58.640 --> 26:00.308
Be careful, Jin Ha-kyung.

26:00.934 --> 26:04.437
I can tell, he goes to women
like they're nothing.

26:07.649 --> 26:10.110
Keep your eyes on the road.
You should focus.

26:11.069 --> 26:13.780
I'm just looking out for you,
like a big brother would've.

26:13.863 --> 26:18.535
Kick Senior Um and that guy,
out of the apartment today. Okay?

26:18.618 --> 26:20.579
Big brother, my ass.

26:21.246 --> 26:24.291
So stay out. And it's not your business.
I'm handling it.

26:50.191 --> 26:52.360
It's so hot.

26:54.321 --> 26:56.781
I heard the computer room

26:56.865 --> 26:59.743
is nice and cold,
because the computer's got new AC.

26:59.826 --> 27:01.244
So how can it be so hot in here?

27:01.328 --> 27:03.705
The computers won't work
if they get too hot.

27:03.788 --> 27:06.833
And they think we can?
They like the machines better than us.

27:07.542 --> 27:10.170
It's so unfair.
With the hours we're putting in?

27:10.253 --> 27:11.838
I'm sure we work just as hard.

27:11.921 --> 27:13.632
That's true.

27:18.845 --> 27:20.138
Yes, this is Yu-jin.

27:29.939 --> 27:33.860
What do you mean the feature article
seems like it'll fall through?

27:33.943 --> 27:36.696
Your husband just called
earlier this morning,

27:36.780 --> 27:38.782
and we discussed things.

27:38.865 --> 27:41.284
According to him,
there's too much on his plate.

27:41.368 --> 27:43.745
Why didn't he turn it down earlier?

27:43.828 --> 27:46.915
The society section's been finalized!
I don't have time for this!

27:46.998 --> 27:49.501
Oh. I'm so sorry.

27:50.418 --> 27:51.378
Uh…

27:52.253 --> 27:54.673
Let me… I'll go talk to him now.

27:55.507 --> 27:57.050
Let me get back to you.

27:57.133 --> 27:58.468
Yes, I'm sorry, sir.

27:59.594 --> 28:00.637
Okay.

28:11.564 --> 28:14.317
Do you know how many computers
are running in here?

28:14.401 --> 28:17.529
And we can't open the windows.
It's like we're being steamed.

28:17.612 --> 28:20.699
Computer room got a new AC,
and it's really cold.

28:20.782 --> 28:22.575
Can't we have that too?

28:23.326 --> 28:24.202
When?

28:27.080 --> 28:29.457
Okay. Please hurry if you can.

28:31.960 --> 28:33.128
Well?

28:33.211 --> 28:35.171
They're here, but we'll have to wait.

28:35.255 --> 28:37.298
They said it'll take a few hours.

28:37.382 --> 28:39.008
Again?

28:39.092 --> 28:41.219
That's what they said an hour ago.

28:41.302 --> 28:42.345
Mm.

28:44.764 --> 28:46.141
Mr. Shin, can you try to negotiate?

28:47.225 --> 28:48.268
Why?

28:48.351 --> 28:50.145
'Cause you're really good at it.

28:55.942 --> 28:57.360
Hey, Lee Si…

29:01.322 --> 29:03.616
Mr. Lee's a little out of it today.

29:04.701 --> 29:07.162
I bet he feels
like he's getting steamed too.

29:09.289 --> 29:10.248
Well, Mr. Shin?

29:10.915 --> 29:12.208
I can go.

29:12.292 --> 29:14.085
No, no.

29:14.169 --> 29:15.712
I'm going.

29:15.795 --> 29:17.422
I'll check it. Okay.

29:19.215 --> 29:20.091
Thank you.

29:24.137 --> 29:26.139
AIR CONDITIONING ROOM
RESTRICTED ACCESS

29:30.727 --> 29:33.021
Hello, I'm from the Chief Team.

29:36.274 --> 29:38.276
Doesn't even sound like they're working.

29:42.155 --> 29:44.115
When will the air conditioner…

29:52.373 --> 29:53.708
Is there something you want?

29:56.336 --> 29:57.712
Ah, yeah.

29:58.671 --> 30:00.757
Thank you for everything. Thanks.

30:12.519 --> 30:13.728
Four toes.

30:14.354 --> 30:15.480
Four.

30:16.648 --> 30:18.858
One, two, three, four.

30:18.942 --> 30:21.653
On their hind legs,
alligators have four toes.

30:30.537 --> 30:31.663
Hey.

30:32.664 --> 30:35.834
The details are almost worked out
for Ha-kyung's blind date.

30:35.917 --> 30:37.794
They'll send a few dates that work,

30:37.877 --> 30:40.338
and then we get to pick
the final date for the date.

30:40.421 --> 30:42.632
Ma, you haven't given up yet?

30:42.715 --> 30:44.509
He's a gynecologist.

30:44.592 --> 30:48.346
So he's got an excellent future
and more than enough money, you know?

30:48.930 --> 30:50.807
Let it go.

30:50.890 --> 30:53.852
It's nearly monsoon season,
I'm sure she's got enough to think about.

30:53.935 --> 30:56.688
If you keep setting things up
without asking,

30:56.771 --> 30:58.481
she will cut you off.

31:00.191 --> 31:04.946
What are you gonna do in life,
when I have another accident and I die?

31:05.029 --> 31:08.157
You and Ha-kyung are hopeless.
You can't do anything.

31:08.241 --> 31:12.370
'Cause when I leave this world,
I wanna know that you both have someone.

31:12.453 --> 31:14.455
Hopefully, they'll handle
planning my funeral.

31:14.539 --> 31:15.456
Mother!

31:15.540 --> 31:16.791
You're fine! Don't say that!

31:16.875 --> 31:21.212
You think your mother will live forever
just to wait on you head and foot?

31:21.296 --> 31:22.672
That's not what I said.

31:22.755 --> 31:25.592
Shut your mouth,
and you can help me or you can hush, okay?

31:25.675 --> 31:26.926
I'll do what I want!

31:27.010 --> 31:29.637
I try to keep you two from fighting,
but I'll knock it off!

31:30.471 --> 31:33.558
You don't know how lucky you are
to have a mom like me.

31:39.314 --> 31:41.983
Why can't she ever let me
get my work done?

31:43.109 --> 31:46.905
Oh, shit. Where was my train
of thought? Shit!

32:12.680 --> 32:15.391
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

32:25.818 --> 32:27.862
Oh, Mr. Lee, you came down?

32:30.615 --> 32:31.866
I have to talk to you.

32:33.409 --> 32:34.327
Okay.

32:37.413 --> 32:38.373
Hm?

32:42.794 --> 32:44.462
HONEY

32:52.428 --> 32:53.805
KI-JUN

33:12.615 --> 33:14.117
OFFICE OF SPOKESPERSON

33:26.713 --> 33:28.423
What's wrong? Are you okay?

33:30.550 --> 33:32.093
I heard there was a car accident.

33:33.011 --> 33:34.012
Are you all right?

33:35.847 --> 33:38.391
Of course. It was a minor accident.
And they towed my car.

33:39.559 --> 33:41.561
Han Ki-jun's suspicious. This was risky.

33:41.644 --> 33:42.812
Maybe I want him to find out.

33:43.563 --> 33:44.397
Huh?

33:44.480 --> 33:46.149
Why did you call Mr. Um?

33:46.232 --> 33:48.359
Why couldn't you text me that you're okay?

33:48.943 --> 33:50.445
I called, so he'd cover me.

33:50.528 --> 33:53.823
Why did Han Ki-jun go
to pick you up, then?

33:55.199 --> 33:56.909
Well, I needed him for my insurance.

33:56.993 --> 33:59.454
How many reasons are there
for Han Ki-jun to see you?

34:00.246 --> 34:01.330
It seems endless.

34:01.414 --> 34:02.832
When is it over?

34:02.915 --> 34:05.376
The column, the apology,
and now car insurance?

34:06.377 --> 34:08.379
I need to know what else is left.

34:12.091 --> 34:13.885
What's been happening with you?

34:13.968 --> 34:16.220
I'm sick and tired of Han Ki-jun.
It's pissing me off!

34:18.347 --> 34:21.934
Do you have any idea how worried I was?

34:23.686 --> 34:26.272
I heard about the accident,
and you weren't responding to me.

34:27.023 --> 34:28.649
If you were hurt,

34:28.733 --> 34:30.777
there was no one I could ask,
how would I know?

34:31.360 --> 34:33.404
I've been worried sick all morning.

34:33.988 --> 34:37.492
The whole meeting, I, I couldn't
do anything but worry about you.

34:39.285 --> 34:41.329
It was impossible
to think of anything else.

34:45.500 --> 34:46.709
In an instant,

34:47.376 --> 34:49.420
it felt like my feelings for you tripled.

34:50.963 --> 34:54.217
But the more they grow,
so do the problems.

34:55.051 --> 34:57.095
And I grow angrier too.

35:00.431 --> 35:03.643
It was nothing but a fender bender,
and everyone was just fine.

35:03.726 --> 35:05.895
I didn't realize
it would worry you like this.

35:09.065 --> 35:10.191
I'm sorry.

35:13.194 --> 35:15.238
You have to stop apologizing.

35:15.321 --> 35:17.156
It makes me feel like I'm the bad guy.

35:17.740 --> 35:19.408
'Cause you really didn't do
anything wrong.

35:35.466 --> 35:37.468
They scheduled a briefing for later today.

35:39.303 --> 35:40.513
You should get ready.

36:08.416 --> 36:09.667
Si-woo.

36:15.006 --> 36:16.174
Can we talk?

36:19.677 --> 36:22.263
- It makes sense. Here.
- Mm.

36:24.432 --> 36:26.809
- So sorry I'm late, everyone.
- Oh, it's fine.

36:26.893 --> 36:28.477
Is everything okay with your car?

36:28.561 --> 36:30.354
And you're, you're okay, right?

36:32.231 --> 36:34.692
- The car needs work, but I'm okay.
- Oh.

36:34.775 --> 36:36.527
I hear there's gonna be
a briefing this afternoon?

36:36.611 --> 36:37.486
Oh.

36:37.570 --> 36:39.739
Can I see the minutes
from the call this morning?

36:39.822 --> 36:41.115
Yeah, of course.

36:41.991 --> 36:45.369
There wasn't anything too out of line
from what we said at the last one.

36:45.912 --> 36:49.790
By Okinawa, there's a stationary front
formed over the sea.

36:49.874 --> 36:52.084
Due to the trough
from northern central China,

36:52.168 --> 36:54.670
combined with the formation of a gale,

36:54.754 --> 36:57.298
it's looking like monsoon season
starts in five days,

36:57.381 --> 36:59.800
and it'll start with Jeju
and parts of the south.

37:01.052 --> 37:02.678
It's just not sitting right with me.

37:03.679 --> 37:04.597
You think it's wrong?

37:04.680 --> 37:08.017
Over Okhotsk Sea,
there's an abnormal anticyclone.

37:08.100 --> 37:10.311
Plus we got cold air
coming down from the north.

37:10.394 --> 37:13.356
If the anticyclone
from the North Pacific weakens,

37:14.023 --> 37:17.818
it'll delay the stationary front
and take longer for it to rise up north.

37:19.570 --> 37:21.197
And what does the data say?

37:21.280 --> 37:22.740
It's almost the same as yesterday.

37:23.407 --> 37:24.492
What do we do?

37:25.368 --> 37:27.161
Your thoughts, Forecaster?

37:34.669 --> 37:37.713
For the briefing, we'll stick
to what was discussed this morning.

37:37.797 --> 37:40.591
I'm not saying I disagree,
it's just if we're changing that much,

37:40.675 --> 37:42.176
we need proof.

37:42.260 --> 37:44.345
Of course. Let's do that.

37:44.428 --> 37:46.055
- Miss Kim.
- Yes, Director?

37:46.138 --> 37:49.183
I need some data on anticipated changes
to that Chinese trough.

37:49.267 --> 37:51.310
- Please send it to the briefing room.
- Yes, ma'am.

38:03.364 --> 38:05.616
What happened with you
and my husband last night?

38:05.700 --> 38:08.744
He found me. He showed up at the door.

38:09.453 --> 38:10.871
My husband came to your house?

38:10.955 --> 38:12.206
To Director Jin's house.

38:12.915 --> 38:14.583
He was already drunk too.

38:14.667 --> 38:17.420
What? Why did he go to her?

38:23.592 --> 38:25.011
Tell me!

38:26.053 --> 38:27.471
I think Ki-jun found out.

38:27.555 --> 38:28.848
What?

38:28.931 --> 38:31.309
That you and I lived together.

38:34.312 --> 38:35.479
Who said so?

38:35.563 --> 38:37.023
You didn't tell him, did you?

38:38.190 --> 38:39.358
You think I would?

38:39.442 --> 38:40.901
I have no reason to.

38:44.238 --> 38:45.239
Oh!

38:46.032 --> 38:48.200
I knew something was wrong.
He's been so weird.

38:48.284 --> 38:49.827
Oh! Oh, no.

38:50.494 --> 38:53.205
It's gonna be fine.
You didn't do anything wrong.

38:53.289 --> 38:55.916
Just tell him it was all
before you knew him.

38:56.584 --> 38:57.793
It's not that simple.

38:58.544 --> 39:00.963
He's not the kind of guy
who just let it go.

39:01.047 --> 39:04.008
I know exactly how he was gonna react,
even though it's in the past.

39:04.091 --> 39:06.093
Oh, it sucks!

39:07.720 --> 39:10.973
We moved in together,
because we loved each other so much.

39:11.766 --> 39:15.936
You said you would never regret
acting out of love. You said that.

39:16.020 --> 39:18.856
Well, love changes,
and my feelings about it changed too.

39:19.774 --> 39:22.526
Back then, I was sure. I knew.
But now it's different.

39:23.152 --> 39:24.779
I'd give anything to change it.

39:25.279 --> 39:26.489
Like you wouldn't?

39:27.073 --> 39:28.199
No.

39:28.282 --> 39:29.658
I don't regret it at all.

39:29.742 --> 39:32.119
'Cause I know what I was doing
what I could.

39:32.203 --> 39:34.955
Sure, you'll think that for now.

39:35.039 --> 39:37.375
When you get a girlfriend,
you'll change your mind.

39:37.458 --> 39:40.002
You'll hate that you used to live with me
at one time then.

39:47.218 --> 39:48.969
Well, I told her.

39:52.515 --> 39:55.643
Wait, you're dating someone, like now?

39:55.726 --> 39:56.977
Yeah.

39:57.561 --> 39:59.271
And I think you should tell him the truth.

39:59.772 --> 40:01.607
When you really love someone,

40:01.690 --> 40:04.026
you love everything,
even things from the past.

40:04.110 --> 40:05.778
He'll move on and accept it.

40:21.669 --> 40:23.546
So hot.

40:25.464 --> 40:26.715
Lee Si-woo.

40:27.383 --> 40:29.301
- Yeah?
- Where did you go?

40:30.761 --> 40:32.012
Something wrong?

40:32.096 --> 40:33.931
You were spacey this morning too.

40:34.014 --> 40:35.850
Seriously, you head's been in the sky.

40:36.434 --> 40:37.726
I'm sorry, sir.

40:37.810 --> 40:40.020
It's the heat.
It's throwing all of us off.

40:40.104 --> 40:41.772
No one's focused with the heat, you know?

40:44.984 --> 40:46.360
Oh, Miss Kim, can I see that?

40:47.653 --> 40:50.030
This is the data predicting
the trough's course.

40:50.114 --> 40:52.408
You can deliver this to the briefing room.

40:52.491 --> 40:54.785
And I know it's hot, still,
you've gotta step up.

40:57.163 --> 40:58.038
Sure.

41:04.795 --> 41:05.880
He could be sick.

41:11.719 --> 41:13.721
It is hot in here.

41:29.778 --> 41:31.363
Is it anyone I've met?

41:33.574 --> 41:35.034
The girl you've been seeing.

41:35.117 --> 41:37.912
She's not anyone that works here, is she?

41:45.711 --> 41:48.297
That's all we can say, currently,
about the start of monsoon season,

41:48.380 --> 41:51.300
I'll pass things to Director Jin Ha-kyung
from Chief Team

41:51.383 --> 41:53.052
to elaborate further and answer questions.

41:59.642 --> 42:01.477
I'm Director Jin from Chief Team Two.

42:01.560 --> 42:03.020
Let's start with questions.

42:06.190 --> 42:08.067
I'm from JBC, Reporter Cho Eun-ji.

42:08.150 --> 42:10.110
Your reports claim
that the seasonal rain front

42:10.194 --> 42:12.488
should last longer than average this year.

42:12.571 --> 42:13.656
Why do you think so?

42:13.739 --> 42:16.450
It has to do with the influence
of the North Pacific's anticyclone.

42:16.534 --> 42:18.994
We think it will reach China
and stay there.

42:19.078 --> 42:21.288
What day do you think
the monsoons will end? Do you know?

42:21.372 --> 42:22.540
Well, we won't state a date.

42:22.623 --> 42:24.625
Probably two or three days later
than average.

42:24.708 --> 42:26.627
Also, I'd like to clarify
some of the terminology.

42:41.642 --> 42:43.978
A significant reason
we're hesitant to give

42:44.061 --> 42:45.646
a predicted end date

42:45.729 --> 42:49.441
is because the weather during the summer
is breaking pattern due to climate change.

42:49.525 --> 42:51.610
In the interest
of avoiding false promises

42:51.694 --> 42:53.696
with start and end dates for the rain,

42:53.779 --> 42:57.157
we've decided that short-range
and weekly forecasts are more appropriate.

43:01.245 --> 43:02.162
For you.

43:05.666 --> 43:07.251
Moving on to the next question.

43:09.670 --> 43:12.756
You're walking with Yu-jin.
Why did that happen?

43:12.840 --> 43:15.509
Well, I don't know.

43:17.428 --> 43:19.680
You don't know? That doesn't make sense.

43:19.763 --> 43:22.808
My history with her is in the past,
so I don't care and I don't know.

43:22.891 --> 43:23.809
Come again?

43:24.560 --> 43:26.312
I understand how to let the past go.

43:26.395 --> 43:30.566
If I found out something I didn't know,
I'd never harass my ex at her house.

43:30.649 --> 43:32.693
You know, that'll make me
seem like a loser.

43:52.630 --> 43:55.633
I heard she was living
with a KMA employee.

43:55.716 --> 43:59.011
I guess she ended up marrying that guy.

43:59.094 --> 44:03.349
Married after living together?
Lived together… Lived together.

44:03.432 --> 44:06.185
Lived together… Lived together…

44:06.977 --> 44:09.647
Lived together… Lived together…

45:05.244 --> 45:06.245
This is all your fault!

45:06.328 --> 45:07.705
And you know it!

45:11.083 --> 45:12.710
Come on, be honest with yourself.

45:12.793 --> 45:15.212
You think you're such a gentleman
while she's in agony?

45:15.295 --> 45:16.714
Just grow up and be a man.

45:16.797 --> 45:17.840
Well, I will.

45:19.717 --> 45:20.551
Hey.

45:26.390 --> 45:27.683
Lee Si-woo, quit it!

45:27.766 --> 45:29.309
Stop them!

45:35.524 --> 45:37.067
Wanna ruin my life, you bastard?

45:37.151 --> 45:38.652
You've really been pissing me off!

45:40.946 --> 45:41.822
Call somebody.

45:41.905 --> 45:43.198
- Hey!
- Let go of me!

45:43.282 --> 45:45.784
Let go!

45:47.619 --> 45:49.371
You have no idea who you're dealing with.

45:49.455 --> 45:51.373
- Let go! Please…
- Stop!

45:51.457 --> 45:52.541
Come on!

45:55.502 --> 45:57.171
FORECAST BUREAU DIRECTOR GENERAL
KO BONG-CHAN

45:57.921 --> 45:59.423
Well done, both of you.

46:06.305 --> 46:07.681
Hm? Great work.

46:11.101 --> 46:12.936
Never did I think we'd sink this low.

46:14.146 --> 46:17.608
I thought weather nerds didn't do
this kind of thing, you proved me wrong.

46:17.691 --> 46:19.777
So, tell me what happened.

46:19.860 --> 46:23.197
What, you two just wanted a fight
in front of the reporters for fun?

46:28.160 --> 46:29.161
Really? Nothing?

46:32.748 --> 46:33.791
Well, okay.

46:34.750 --> 46:35.626
Hey, Mr. Park.

46:36.210 --> 46:37.085
Yes?

46:37.169 --> 46:41.048
I want written apologies from those two,
and whatever else HR says.

46:41.548 --> 46:42.591
Yes, sir.

46:47.554 --> 46:49.431
On today, of all days.

47:04.822 --> 47:06.573
What do you think made them fight?

47:06.657 --> 47:09.743
It's so hot outside. We have no AC inside.

47:09.827 --> 47:12.621
No, they wouldn't fight,
just 'cause they're too warm.

47:13.789 --> 47:15.457
Not in front of that many people.

47:19.670 --> 47:21.171
I have tea.

47:22.089 --> 47:23.632
You know Mr. Han's wife, right?

47:23.715 --> 47:24.716
The reporter?

47:24.800 --> 47:28.053
Well, can you guess
who in the building is her ex-boyfriend?

47:30.138 --> 47:31.139
You're kidding.

47:31.223 --> 47:32.266
It's true.

47:32.349 --> 47:35.060
- But it's true. Lee Si-woo dated her.
- Whoa!

47:39.690 --> 47:40.774
Seriously?

47:41.650 --> 47:43.151
Wait, hang on.

47:43.861 --> 47:47.406
Then her husband and her ex have been
working together every day,

47:47.489 --> 47:49.741
and they couldn't take it
and fought over her?

47:50.325 --> 47:52.619
But why? She already married Mr. Han.

47:53.203 --> 47:55.038
Maybe she cheated on him with Lee Si-woo.

47:56.248 --> 47:57.916
I don't think so.

47:58.000 --> 48:00.836
Si-woo's too willing to stick
to his guns and that.

48:01.795 --> 48:04.798
There's no way he'd go back
to a relationship that ended a while ago.

48:05.632 --> 48:08.677
I think there's something else
bothering him.

48:08.760 --> 48:10.262
Okay, but what would that be?

48:10.345 --> 48:11.555
Okay, what do you know?

48:12.139 --> 48:13.265
If I had to guess…

48:14.266 --> 48:16.518
If someone was baiting the other,
it was Han Ki-jun.

48:17.561 --> 48:19.688
I'd know. After ten years, I can say.

48:20.689 --> 48:21.815
He's irrational.

48:23.233 --> 48:24.401
Mm.

48:25.152 --> 48:28.447
So I think it'd be best
if all of us didn't bring it up again.

48:28.530 --> 48:31.867
Lee Si-woo's struggling today.
And I expect you all to respect that.

48:33.702 --> 48:34.661
Of course.

48:34.745 --> 48:37.831
Dissecting the love lives
of our co-workers isn't work our time.

48:37.915 --> 48:41.627
And so, huh,
it won't come up again, director.

48:42.377 --> 48:43.211
It's over.

48:49.259 --> 48:50.260
Yeah. Whatever.

48:51.011 --> 48:52.846
- Hm.
- Hm.

49:05.067 --> 49:06.860
Oh, the AC's on.

49:06.944 --> 49:07.819
Oh!

49:10.030 --> 49:11.782
Hey, so whatever you said to them worked.

49:12.991 --> 49:15.744
I just didn't do anything, really.

49:19.122 --> 49:20.749
Thanks for your help.

49:21.500 --> 49:22.709
Specially in this heat.

49:22.793 --> 49:24.169
- Oh, thank you.
- Here.

49:24.252 --> 49:25.545
Thank you.

49:25.629 --> 49:27.089
Great.

49:28.382 --> 49:30.467
Please take one. Yeah.

49:30.550 --> 49:31.802
Oh, thank you.

49:32.427 --> 49:33.345
Oh, gosh.

49:34.096 --> 49:35.514
That'll do.

49:35.597 --> 49:37.683
- Wow, that's nice.
- Yeah.

49:48.443 --> 49:50.320
Oh, this is…

49:50.404 --> 49:52.114
UPCOMING RAINY SEASON
WILL BE HOT AND WORSE

49:52.197 --> 49:53.991
LOCAL GOVERNMENTS PREPARE
FOR THE RAINY SEASON

50:39.745 --> 50:40.996
Why her?

50:46.209 --> 50:48.420
We wrapped out, so I'm heading out.

50:48.503 --> 50:49.713
Miss Lee.

50:49.796 --> 50:50.881
Take this.

50:51.506 --> 50:52.424
Oh.

50:53.175 --> 50:55.761
We can just do the usual transfer,
it's fine.

50:55.844 --> 50:58.388
I've already sent payment for this month.

50:58.472 --> 51:00.265
Think of this like a tip.

51:01.058 --> 51:03.268
Oh, you're too kind.

51:05.020 --> 51:08.607
By the way, have something been
happening at home recently?

51:09.441 --> 51:11.359
Uh, no. Why?

51:11.443 --> 51:16.239
My kid said that teacher was distracted
in the lessons lately, so…

51:17.532 --> 51:18.533
Oh.

51:18.617 --> 51:21.244
You know, kids pick up
on more than we think.

51:21.328 --> 51:23.205
So I hope everything's okay.

51:24.247 --> 51:26.416
Yeah. I apologize, ma'am.

51:27.542 --> 51:28.919
See you next week.

51:29.002 --> 51:30.754
Okay. Get home safe.

52:15.590 --> 52:19.427
CALLS

52:19.511 --> 52:22.264
BO-MI'S DAD

52:33.733 --> 52:36.153
KMA ANNOUNCES
THIS YEAR'S RAINY SEASON PROSPECT

52:48.957 --> 52:50.542
WIFE

52:54.004 --> 52:56.339
- Hey, how are you?
- Where are you?

52:57.799 --> 52:59.759
At the KMA, like always.

52:59.843 --> 53:00.969
Where in the building?

53:02.095 --> 53:03.346
Night-duty room.

53:04.222 --> 53:05.390
Is it comfortable enough?

53:06.224 --> 53:07.142
Well…

53:07.726 --> 53:10.103
I hardly think about it. We're so busy.

53:10.770 --> 53:13.982
Today was chaotic, we've out of break,
'cause we announced the rainy season.

53:14.065 --> 53:15.567
It's my first break today.

53:16.526 --> 53:17.694
It must be hard.

53:18.570 --> 53:20.447
Uh, it's fine.

53:21.781 --> 53:22.741
Ah.

53:24.910 --> 53:26.244
Okay, then. See you.

53:26.828 --> 53:28.580
Oh, um, is Bo-mi doing…

53:50.101 --> 53:51.269
He said what?

53:51.353 --> 53:53.396
Mr. Um went home hours ago.

53:54.147 --> 53:55.440
Oh, yes.

53:55.523 --> 53:57.400
He's not here. He left a while ago.

53:59.653 --> 54:01.655
Well, then I better get home, huh.

54:01.738 --> 54:03.073
Thanks for everything.

54:03.907 --> 54:05.492
Of course. Good evening.

54:31.685 --> 54:32.811
Jeez.

54:40.986 --> 54:41.945
Come on!

54:54.374 --> 54:55.292
Here.

54:56.584 --> 54:57.669
Ah!

54:57.752 --> 55:00.130
Aw, I didn't know you were so sensitive.

55:01.256 --> 55:03.174
So, are you upset?

55:03.717 --> 55:05.302
You don't approve if you're asking.

55:05.385 --> 55:08.138
He started it. What did you want me to do?
He starts punching.

55:08.221 --> 55:09.514
Do I just stand there?

55:12.017 --> 55:13.226
Well, it's not his fault.

55:15.854 --> 55:18.148
The columns and the insurance
are my doing.

55:18.231 --> 55:20.442
And I know it's strange
that I still call him.

55:20.525 --> 55:23.820
Ten years together, it left us entangled
in unexpected ways.

55:24.404 --> 55:27.198
And there are certain things
I can't cut off quite so easily.

55:29.576 --> 55:31.494
What happened this morning was,

55:32.078 --> 55:34.122
that he changed my insurance
without telling me,

55:34.205 --> 55:35.957
so his friend would get the commission.

55:36.041 --> 55:38.001
And in the moment, I was so stressed.

55:38.084 --> 55:40.712
The man in the other car kept yelling
about my insurance.

55:43.048 --> 55:46.051
And I thought if I left out
all these little details for you,

55:46.676 --> 55:49.429
that you might not judge me,
that you wouldn't know

55:50.221 --> 55:52.265
that my last relationship was so awful.

55:52.891 --> 55:54.100
And I could forget.

55:55.101 --> 55:56.227
So then…

55:57.437 --> 55:58.688
Why are you telling me this now?

56:01.066 --> 56:03.276
Well, I'd rather be embarrassed
for a second

56:03.902 --> 56:05.695
than have you wonder

56:06.571 --> 56:08.990
if I'm tricking you,
I'd rather have trust.

56:13.953 --> 56:16.539
Starting now,
you're getting total honesty.

56:17.957 --> 56:22.962
I can't promise exactly when all
of the pieces of Han Ki-jun will be gone

56:23.046 --> 56:24.339
and in my past.

56:25.632 --> 56:28.676
All I can say is that in the future,
I will share everything with you.

56:29.636 --> 56:30.970
I'm an open book.

56:31.554 --> 56:32.472
So…

56:39.396 --> 56:40.855
This is getting out of hand.

56:42.649 --> 56:43.983
What are you feeling?

56:46.277 --> 56:49.239
I like you more than anyone I've known.

56:50.657 --> 56:52.367
And that's a little scary.

56:57.414 --> 57:00.959
It's getting to the point where I want
everyone to catch us and find out.

57:02.293 --> 57:05.505
Well, it's gonna be an issue,
'cause we'd have to call it off.

57:13.304 --> 57:15.140
What the… What if they saw you?

57:15.723 --> 57:17.267
It's not work. We're fine.

57:17.350 --> 57:19.060
It's a small world. You'll never know.

57:20.728 --> 57:22.355
If you're worried about appearances,

57:22.439 --> 57:26.025
you shouldn't even look at me,
'cause they can see it in your eyes.

57:26.109 --> 57:27.235
Jin Ha-kyung.

57:29.612 --> 57:31.322
"Jin Ha…" So…

57:33.324 --> 57:34.284
You're crazy!

58:00.185 --> 58:01.436
There's no way.

58:17.327 --> 58:18.244
What's going on?

58:21.289 --> 58:22.665
You have something to tell me.

58:23.875 --> 58:24.918
Don't you?

58:28.546 --> 58:30.507
I'm tired. Later.

58:31.758 --> 58:33.468
We used to live together.

58:35.553 --> 58:38.389
We had an apartment. We dated a while ago.

58:38.973 --> 58:40.058
Is that so wrong?

58:40.683 --> 58:44.062
Well, that was before I knew you.
It's not that bad.

58:44.145 --> 58:46.022
There's nothing wrong
with living together.

58:47.524 --> 58:48.691
No, there's…

58:57.534 --> 58:59.118
You're right. There isn't.

58:59.202 --> 59:02.205
It's not illegal.
I don't think it's even unethical.

59:02.288 --> 59:03.957
I know that.

59:04.040 --> 59:06.125
It's killing me still, Yu-jin.

59:07.961 --> 59:09.420
"I wish I never knew."

59:09.504 --> 59:12.131
"Just pretend you didn't hear.
Pretend you don't know."

59:13.591 --> 59:15.802
It's stuck and there's nothing I can do.

59:17.845 --> 59:20.557
I just can't deal with how you used to…

59:22.183 --> 59:24.185
live with someone else.
You get it, Yu-jin?

59:25.019 --> 59:27.939
And the fact that it was Lee Si-woo
kills me most of all.

59:29.190 --> 59:31.317
It was before I met you.

59:31.401 --> 59:32.944
Leave the past. Think about now.

59:33.027 --> 59:35.154
It's not over. If it were, maybe I could.

59:35.238 --> 59:37.532
What do you mean? I'm totally over him.

59:37.615 --> 59:38.866
Yu-jin, do you…

59:42.078 --> 59:43.121
Shit.

59:45.790 --> 59:48.418
Do you know
who Lee Si-woo's dating right now?

59:50.086 --> 59:53.298
Bad weather isn't
as obvious as cloudy skies,

59:53.381 --> 59:57.760
unexpected snow and rain,
strong wind, and typhoons.

59:57.844 --> 59:59.429
It can be more subtle.

01:00:00.346 --> 01:00:02.307
So who's he dating?

01:00:05.893 --> 01:00:07.103
Jin Ha-kyung.

01:00:12.275 --> 01:00:13.359
Huh?

01:00:14.277 --> 01:00:15.153
Who's that?

01:00:15.236 --> 01:00:16.696
My ex-fiancée.

01:00:17.322 --> 01:00:19.490
The woman I spent ten years with.

01:00:20.074 --> 01:00:21.826
Director Jin Ha-kyung from Team Two!

01:00:31.836 --> 01:00:34.088
Just like that,
we've been transformed,

01:00:35.340 --> 01:00:37.967
irritable and unaware
that it's the weather's doing.

01:00:49.812 --> 01:00:53.858
If onlyit was as obvious
as a total downpour.

01:01:10.124 --> 01:01:12.627
Well, that's not rain. Told ya.

01:01:16.464 --> 01:01:19.550
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

01:01:52.542 --> 01:01:54.585
- Are you dating Lee Si-woo?
- What?

01:01:54.669 --> 01:01:57.130
Aren't you just jealous,
because they're going out?

01:01:57.213 --> 01:01:59.048
Jealous? Of Si-woo?

01:01:59.132 --> 01:02:00.758
Why don't we just
let everyone know?

01:02:00.842 --> 01:02:02.051
We have to play innocent.

01:02:03.261 --> 01:02:07.140
I'm sure that bastard Si-woo
approached Ha-kyung to get back at me.

01:02:08.266 --> 01:02:09.934
How is it coming along?

01:02:10.017 --> 01:02:12.562
Isn't making hasty conclusions
your specialty?

01:02:12.645 --> 01:02:14.731
Why don't you two have a debate about it?

01:02:15.898 --> 01:02:17.024
You should stop seeing her.

01:02:17.608 --> 01:02:19.777
Ha-kyung
doesn't date anyone sincerely

01:02:19.861 --> 01:02:21.571
unless they're a marriage prospect.
